{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "L{t^2*e^(-t)}(s) = 2/(s + 1)^3\n  region of convergence: Re(s) > -1\n  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)\n  rules: e^(at) f(t) -> F(s - a), t^n f(t) -> (-1)^n F^(n)(s)\n  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = -1/2, 1/2, 3: max relative difference 4.4e-16\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "laplace", "ucas": "laplace t^2*e^(-t)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "laplace", "region_of_convergence": "Re(s) > -1", "roc": "Re(s) > -1", "one_sided": "f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)", "rules": "e^(at) f(t) -> F(s - a), t^n f(t) -> (-1)^n F^(n)(s)", "lhs": "L{t^2*e^(-t)}(s)", "value": "2/(s + 1)^3", "headline": "L{t^2*e^(-t)}(s) = 2/(s + 1)^3"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = -1/2, 1/2, 3: max relative difference 4.4e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "L{t^2*e^(-t)}(s) = 2/(s + 1)^3\n  region of convergence: Re(s) > -1\n  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)\n  rules: e^(at) f(t) -> F(s - a), t^n f(t) -> (-1)^n F^(n)(s)\n  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = -1/2, 1/2, 3: max relative difference 4.4e-16\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 1)}(t) = sin(t)\n  poles: s = +-i\n  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)\n  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 1.8e-16\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "ilaplace", "ucas": "ilaplace 1/(s^2+1)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ilaplace", "poles": "s = +-i", "roc": "Re(s) > 0", "lhs": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 1)}(t)", "value": "sin(t)", "headline": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 1)}(t) = sin(t)", "details": ["for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 1.8e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 1)}(t) = sin(t)\n  poles: s = +-i\n  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)\n  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 1.8e-16\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Z{a^n}(z) = z/(z - a)\n  region of convergence: |z| > abs(a)\n  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0\n  rules: a^n x[n] -> X(z/a)\n  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (88 terms) at z = 17/10, 17/5, 71/10 with a = 7/10: max relative difference 2e-16\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "ztrans", "ucas": "ztrans a^n", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ztrans", "region_of_convergence": "|z| > abs(a)", "roc": "|z| > abs(a)", "one_sided": "x[n] for n >= 0", "rules": "a^n x[n] -> X(z/a)", "lhs": "Z{a^n}(z)", "value": "z/(z - a)", "headline": "Z{a^n}(z) = z/(z - a)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (88 terms) at z = 17/10, 17/5, 71/10 with a = 7/10: max relative difference 2e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "Z{a^n}(z) = z/(z - a)\n  region of convergence: |z| > abs(a)\n  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0\n  rules: a^n x[n] -> X(z/a)\n  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (88 terms) at z = 17/10, 17/5, 71/10 with a = 7/10: max relative difference 2e-16\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "F{e^(-x^2)}(w) = sqrt(pi)*e^(-w^2/4)\n  convention: F(w) = int f(x) e^(-iwx) dx over the real line (angular frequency; the inverse has 1/(2pi))\n  check: matches the integral computed numerically at w = 1/2, 13/10, 27/10: max relative difference 6.7e-16\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "fourier", "ucas": "fourier e^(-x^2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "fourier", "convention": "F(w) = int f(x) e^(-iwx) dx over the real line (angular frequency; the inverse has 1/(2pi))", "lhs": "F{e^(-x^2)}(w)", "value": "sqrt(pi)*e^(-w^2/4)", "headline": "F{e^(-x^2)}(w) = sqrt(pi)*e^(-w^2/4)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches the integral computed numerically at w = 1/2, 13/10, 27/10: max relative difference 6.7e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "F{e^(-x^2)}(w) = sqrt(pi)*e^(-w^2/4)\n  convention: F(w) = int f(x) e^(-iwx) dx over the real line (angular frequency; the inverse has 1/(2pi))\n  check: matches the integral computed numerically at w = 1/2, 13/10, 27/10: max relative difference 6.7e-16\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)\n  converges absolutely: p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1\n  = pi^2/6\n  method: partial fractions; zeta(k), digamma at integers\n  numeric: 1.644934066848226 (the first 128 terms plus an Euler-Maclaurin tail (integral + 3 corrections); estimated error 4.4e-16)\n  check: the closed form and the numeric value agree (difference 4.4e-16)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "infinite_sum", "ucas": "sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "infinite_sum", "converges_absolutely": "p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1", "value": "pi^2/6", "method": "partial fractions; zeta(k), digamma at integers", "numeric": "1.644934066848226 (the first 128 terms plus an Euler-Maclaurin tail (integral + 3 corrections); estimated error 4.4e-16)", "headline": "sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the closed form and the numeric value agree (difference 4.4e-16)"}], "files": [], "text": "sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)\n  converges absolutely: p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1\n  = pi^2/6\n  method: partial fractions; zeta(k), digamma at integers\n  numeric: 1.644934066848226 (the first 128 terms plus an Euler-Maclaurin tail (integral + 3 corrections); estimated error 4.4e-16)\n  check: the closed form and the numeric value agree (difference 4.4e-16)\n"}, "isError": false}}
